{"id":"n-20261017-6qv0tv","category":"world","display_title":"Trump Claims Abraham Accords Revived","display_title_he":"טראמפ טוען: הסכמי אברהם חזרו לשולחן","short_summary":"Donald Trump claimed that expanding the Abraham Accords to Saudi Arabia is back on the table amid shared security concerns. However, diplomatic observers note persistent political hurdles.","english_level":"C1","words":462,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Ynet","domain":"ynet.co.il","url":"https://www.ynet.co.il/news/article/ryzrlje3mg","title":"טראמפ: הסכמי אברהם חזרו לשולחן, ישראל סייעה לסעודיה נגד החות׳ים","published_at":"2026-10-16T17:41:05.000Z"},{"name":"Walla","domain":"walla.co.il","url":"https://www.walla.co.il/news/world/383957731","title":"ישראל מסייעת לסעודיה נגד החות’ים - הסכמי אברהם חוזרים","published_at":"2026-10-16T17:40:48.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-16T17:40:48.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-17T05:34:56.120Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Speaking to reporters prior to boarding a flight for a campaign rally in Georgia, Donald Trump asserted that the diplomatic initiative to bring Saudi Arabia into the Abraham Accords is once again being actively considered. When questioned about whether formal normalization had returned to the negotiating agenda, Trump offered an affirmative response, suggesting the prospect was perhaps stronger than ever before. He added that the Saudi leadership was exceedingly pleased with defensive backing provided by both the United States and Israel.","Trump maintained that Israel had provided substantial assistance to Saudi Arabia in counteracting persistent attacks by Houthi insurgents. While the American leader declined to detail the precise operational scope of this cooperation, reports indicate that Israeli support has concentrated primarily on targeting intelligence. Observers note that while Riyadh might desire access to advanced Israeli air defense architecture, such transfers would realistically be evaluated only if the kingdom officially joined the accords. Furthermore, Washington had earlier made a proposed civil nuclear arrangement conditional upon Saudi normalization with Israel.","Beneath this diplomatic rhetoric, substantial political obstacles endure. Insiders indicate that Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman harbors profound skepticism toward Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. According to regional analysts, Riyadh and other Arab capitals are closely monitoring political developments in Israel, effectively awaiting future electoral outcomes before committing to historic shifts. Most crucially, the kingdom has reiterated its foundational prerequisite: normalization remains contingent upon a credible, irreversible diplomatic process leading toward a sovereign Palestinian state.","Concurrently, Prime Minister Netanyahu has reportedly sought American mediation to formalize security coordination against the Houthis, seeking to cultivate strategic goodwill. Nevertheless, a diplomatic source cited in Haaretz indicated that Crown Prince Mohammed vetoed direct Israeli military involvement in Yemen, mindful of domestic public opinion.","These geopolitical deliberations coincide with a sharp military escalation between Saudi Arabia and Houthi fighters. Riyadh has long attempted to downplay the operational consequences of insurgent strikes, strictly curbing public documentation and projecting an image of commercial stability. However, recent strikes have complicated these efforts. A significant strike targeting King Khalid International Airport in Riyadh briefly disrupted aviation operations at a crucial gateway for foreign investors and business leaders.","The timing is especially sensitive, as the kingdom prepares to host its flagship Future Investment Initiative summit between October 26 and October 29. Analysts emphasize that the Houthis are deliberately targeting vulnerable economic arteries to disrupt Saudi Arabia's Vision 2030, an ambitious modernization blueprint designed to transform the kingdom into an international hub for finance, technology, and logistics. Farea al-Muslimi, a researcher at the British think tank Chatham House, remarked that the insurgents recognize Saudi vulnerability in its economic reputation. While some commentators argue that economic disruption will subside once broader regional tensions de-escalate, the ongoing turmoil underscores the fragile foundation upon which regional diplomacy currently rests."],"facts":[{"fact":"Speaking to reporters before departing for a campaign rally in Georgia, Donald Trump stated that expanding the Abraham Accords to include Saudi Arabia is back on the table, possibly more than ever.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Trump claimed that Israel has provided significant assistance to Saudi Arabia in its confrontation with Houthi rebels, and that Riyadh is pleased with support from both Israel and the United States.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Israeli assistance to Saudi Arabia has focused primarily on targeting intelligence, while any future provision of advanced Israeli air defense systems would depend on Riyadh formally joining the Abraham Accords.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"According to diplomatic sources, Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman lacks trust in Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and maintains that diplomatic normalization remains conditional on establishing an irreversible political path toward an independent Palestinian state.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"A diplomatic source reported in Haaretz that Netanyahu has sought American mediation to intervene in the Houthi conflict to foster ties, but Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman placed a veto on direct Israeli military intervention due to domestic public opinion.","sources":[2]},{"fact":"Recent Houthi strikes, notably an attack disabling King Khalid International Airport in Riyadh, have escalated economic pressures on Saudi Arabia 